though there have been many attempts to come up with some sort of like theoretical principled way of figuring out how to do mixtures the reality is that today you have to basically just run experiments So you say, okay I want my model", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/_lewtun/status/2094364485871923547#t=3721", "end": 3840.582, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "d502cc0df05e6fc88d8be587b2713a99ef63d8057718a4515fa20762b93c822e", "start": 3721.393, "text": "you think of them in the abstract and you'll look at like some spec sheet from NVIDIA and you'll say okay, here's like the theoretical flops I can get from my from this GPU I'll do some benchmarking on the GPU and then you know, I'll say, o", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/_lewtun/status/2094364485871923547#t=5358", "end": 5477.815, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "321e1e9d1d74836a5923860efff6047f41680b2d1d550f7dfce060d07e95ac5e", "start": 5358.348, "text": "It exploited that to basically launch a cyber attack on Hugging Face because it thought oh the answer to my question is probably on Hugging Face because we host all the public benchmarks And these benchmarks are typically private because yo", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "AI and ML", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/_lewtun/status/2094364485871923547#t=315", "end": 434.364, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "1288b9169eff2925bbb6b7c5af0edf8dd91774864f4c742d4da33b7d103975e1", "start": 315.354, "text": "such as in-context learning where if you just provided the model with a sequence of examples it could then figure out how to autocomplete the final example. So if you look here you've got this model you just give it a bunch of addition prob", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/_lewtun/status/2094364485871923547#t=1461", "end": 1580.863,